From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:25:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: Enter L0 before calling the resume
 callback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the controller leaves clock gating or LPM L1, dwc2 calls the
gadget driver's resume callback first and only then sets lx_state to
L0. call_gadget() drops the controller lock around the callback, and a
function driver may queue a request from it right away (CDC ACM and
ECM send their notifications on resume). dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses
requests while lx_state is not L0, so these requests fail with -EAGAIN
and the notification is lost. From L1, the queue path even tries to
wake the controller from L1 a second time.

Set lx_state to L0 and clear bus_suspended before calling the resume
callback.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 7dcb77b9 and omarchy-ipad5
 patches/periph/usb-resume/0001 (J71t ledger 7.1); applied the same
 reordering to the LPM L1 exit in dwc2_wakeup_from_lpm_l1(), which had
 the same order]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c | 6 +++---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c    | 8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
index 9565e6a52..0be67f27d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
@@ -390,11 +390,11 @@ void dwc2_wakeup_from_lpm_l1(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, bool remotewakeup)
 			return;
 		}
 
-		/* Inform gadget to exit from L1 */
-		call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
-		/* Change to L0 state */
+		/* Change to L0 state before informing the gadget */
 		hsotg->lx_state = DWC2_L0;
 		hsotg->bus_suspended = false;
+		/* Inform gadget to exit from L1 */
+		call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
 fail:		dwc2_gadget_init_lpm(hsotg);
 	} else {
 		/* TODO */
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
index 102169b40..07220a0bc 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -5741,8 +5741,12 @@ void dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, int rem_wakeup)
 		dwc2_writel(hsotg, dctl, DCTL);
 	}
 
-	/* Change to L0 state */
-	call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
+	/*
+	 * Change to L0 state before the resume callback: it may queue
+	 * requests right away, and dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses them
+	 * outside L0.
+	 */
 	hsotg->lx_state = DWC2_L0;
 	hsotg->bus_suspended = false;
+	call_gadget(hsotg, resume);
 }
